# 7. Job ownership, process safety, and cancellation

## 7.1 Process ownership

Every subprocess started by a run MUST be attributable to that run. A persisted PID alone MUST NOT be treated as durable ownership evidence.

Run-owned subprocesses MUST be isolated using an OS process group/job object or an equivalent process identity that prevents stale PID reuse from authorizing termination. The implementation MAY use platform-specific mechanisms; the invariant is reliable run ownership, not a mandated API.

20. canary credentials do not appear in persisted failure evidence;
21. equivalent CLI/Web requests normalize to equivalent config/stage semantics;
22. full-stream decode rejects corrupt-tail and missing-audio outputs;
23. crash after N-of-M expensive assets resumes without regenerating the verified N.

