# 12. Golden acceptance

A release/product revision is accepted only after a real Golden CUJ passes against a **predeclared canonical Golden fixture manifest committed to the accepted source revision**.

The fixture manifest MUST identify exact input hashes and MUST exercise:

- narration duration longer than the F2 opening interval;
- at least one subtitle before and after `00:30`;
- the real selected provider path;
- post-opening composition;
- final program tail;
- rerun/reuse behavior.

The fixture MUST NOT be selected or shortened merely to make the current implementation pass.

The Golden CUJ MUST record:

```text
exact clean Git revision
input hashes
effective configuration fingerprint
creative_plan_fingerprint
format_id + format_plan_fingerprint
editorial_timeline_fingerprint
effect_profile_fingerprint
provider mode + provider attempt/job/output identity when available
run_id
stage evidence
format-grammar validation evidence
visual-coverage evidence
final artifact path
final SHA-256
media probe result
full decode result
```

The Golden evidence bundle MUST include observation points inside the opening, immediately after the opening boundary, at program midpoint, and near the final program tail. These observations are owner-observable evidence for product-semantic visual behavior; machine verification remains responsible for identity, timing, streams, coverage, secrets, cancellation, and provenance.

## 12.1 Acceptance criteria

For the canonical representative story fixture:

- preflight succeeds or truthfully stops before the first externally expensive/paid operation;
- one Run invocation traverses all required stages;
- the selected F1–F5 format has intentional visual coverage and passes machine format-grammar validation;
- F2 follows the current Flow/Veo generated-opening contract and BOTH_CLASSES_REQUIRED post-opening mix semantics;
- equivalent Web and CLI requests use the same product core and normalize to equivalent output-affecting semantics;
- final video contains required streams and fully decodes through EOF;
- final duration matches authoritative audio within the normative §4.2 tolerance;
- final artifact has exact provenance to clean source/config/input/CreativePlan/FormatPlan/EditorialTimeline/run;
- an identical rerun safely reuses identity-matching work, while any nondeterministic provider regeneration remains separately attributed rather than called byte-deterministic;
- a changed output-affecting input/config invalidates the affected cached artifacts;
- cancel does not kill unrelated FFmpeg/process work;
- remote cancellation state is reported truthfully;
- no secrets are present in tracked files or durable evidence;
- docs describe the implementation that actually ran;
- the literal canonical verification command passes on the accepted revision.

Passing unit tests without this journey is not Product Acceptance.

